[Desktop Entry]
Name=Phosh
Comment=Phone Shell
Comment=This session logs you into Phosh
# e5-linux: phoc has to be told to use wlroots' GLES2 renderer without touching
# the binary (an overlay copy of /usr/bin/phoc would have to carry a copy of the
# binary too, because the real one has to stay available as phoc.orig).
# WLR_RENDERER is *set* rather than left to wlroots' default so that an
# /etc/environment still carrying WLR_RENDERER=pixman cannot win.
#
# What is deliberately not done here: splitting scanout from rendering with
# WLR_DRM_DEVICES=/dev/dri/card0:/dev/dri/renderD128.  It is the shape this
# hardware wants -- allocate on panfrost, import into the vendor KMS driver --
# but with libseat/logind wlroots cannot open the devices from an explicit list
# on this device ("Unable to open /dev/dri/card0 as KMS device", "Found 0 GPUs,
# cannot create backend" and no session at all), so wlroots stays on its default
# path: Mesa's kmsro renders on panfrost and the *display* device allocates the
# swapchain with its own dumb buffers.  That is why
# drivers/unisoc_platform/sprd_disp/sprd_gem.c's ten-dumb-buffers-per-boot cap
# had to be raised.  See docs/FINDINGS.md section 20.7.
Exec=env WLR_RENDERER=gles2 phosh-session
Type=Application
DesktopNames=Phosh;GNOME;
